                                "sense_id": "57e5272f-ffa4-3545-9100-8665392e84b4",
                                "text": "The ureteral catheters are passed through the holes and down toward the anus. Mucosa-to-mucosa ureteroproctostomies are made over the catheters with atraumatic chromic catgut. The catheters insure patency, prevent reflux, and temporarily divert urine from the suture line."
